    "roles": ["session", "band_member", "producer", "bandleader"],
    "summary": "English session drummer, producer and bandleader. He played in his father Sid Phillips's Dixieland band from twelve and was a London session player by his late teens. On Judas Priest's Sin After Sin (1977) he brought two bass drums into heavy metal; then Jeff Beck's There & Back, the Michael Schenker Group's first album and Mike Oldfield's Crises, which he co-produced. Toto's drummer from 1992 to 2014, then Hiromi's Trio Project and his own Protocol records. Right-handed, he plays open-handed, the left hand on the hat, and behind two 24-inch bass drums."
  },
